---
import MuMpcLogo from '../../../components/MuMpcLogo.astro';
import videoUrl from './muMPC_full.mp4?url';
import rolloutUrl from './method_videos/01-latent-rollout.mp4?url';
import programUrl from './method_videos/02-condensed-program.mp4?url';
import solverUrl from './method_videos/03-primal-dual-solver.mp4?url';
import diffQpUrl from './method_videos/04-diffQP.mp4?url';
import robotariumUrl from './result_videos/robotarium_clipped_2x.mp4?url';
import swarmUrl from './result_videos/noref_plan_ibr_ego_left_to_right_2x.mp4?url';
import quadrupedNomUrl from './result_videos/go2_nom_side.mp4?url';
import quadrupedObsUrl from './result_videos/go2_obs_top_down.mp4?url';
import crazyflieUrl from './result_videos/cf_mpc_2x2.mp4?url';
import cubeUrl from './result_videos/cube_real_diffqp_comparison.mp4?url';
import ropeUrl from './result_videos/rope_mpc_2x2.mp4?url';
const methodSteps = [
  { title: 'Precompute the latent rollout', url: rolloutUrl, explanation: 'A learned encoder lifts the measured state into linear latent dynamics. μMPC compiles these dynamics into maps from the initial state and control sequence to future outputs. The maps are built offline for a fixed model and horizon, so online prediction needs only one state encoding and matrix–vector products.' },
  { title: 'Condense the quadratic program', url: programUrl, explanation: 'Substituting the prediction maps into the objective and constraints leaves only the control sequence to optimize. The QP size depends on the horizon and input dimension, not the latent dimension. New goals change only the linear objective term; locally linearized constraints become inequalities on the controls, tightened for approximation error.' },
  { title: 'Solve with a frozen inverse', url: solverUrl, explanation: 'A primal–dual solver updates constraint multipliers by projection and controls through a precomputed inverse. For fixed model, horizon, weights, and regularization, this inverse is reused as goals and constraints change. Each iteration needs only matrix–vector products and projections. This moves expensive matrix inversion and factorization offline, keeping online updates lightweight.' },
  { title: 'Learn through differentiable control', url: diffQpUrl, explanation: 'A differentiable tracking QP recovers the actions needed to reproduce demonstrated trajectories. Comparing these actions with demonstrations trains the encoder and dynamics for control, alongside prediction losses. DAgger-style aggregation adds simulated trajectories from the tracking controller, helping the model learn on the states its own controller visits.' },
];
const subtitle = 'Safe Nonlinear and World Model Control in Microseconds via Koopman-Linearized Pre-Compilation';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#151515" />
    <meta name="description" content={subtitle} />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" sizes="any" href="/projects/micrompc/favicon.svg" />
    <title>μMPC</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header>
        <h1><MuMpcLogo /></h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Safe Nonlinear and World Model Control in <span class="highlight">Microseconds</span> via Koopman-Linearized Pre-Compilation</p>
        <p class="authors"><a href="/">Devesh Nath</a><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Glen Chou</span></p>
        <nav aria-label="Project resources">
          {[
            { label: 'Paper', path: 'M14 3H6v18h12V7l-4-4Z M14 3v5h4 M9 12h6 M9 16h6' },
            { label: 'Code', path: 'm8 7-5 5 5 5 M16 7l5 5-5 5 M14 4l-4 16' },
            { label: 'Video', path: 'm8 5 11 7-11 7V5Z' },
          ].map(({ label, path }) => (
            label === 'Video' ? (
              <a href="#video" aria-label="Watch the summary video"><span class="resource-label"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d={path} /></svg><span>{label}</span></span></a>
            ) : (
            <button type="button" aria-disabled="true" aria-label={`${label}: Coming Soon!`}>
              <span class="resource-label" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={path} /></svg><span>{label}</span></span>
              <span class="soon" aria-hidden="true">Coming Soon!</span>
            </button>
            )
          ))}
        </nav>
      </header>
      <section id="video" aria-label="μMPC full presentation">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <video controls autoplay muted playsinline preload="auto" aria-label="μMPC full presentation video">
          <source src={videoUrl} type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support embedded video. <a href={videoUrl}>Download the video</a>.
        </video>
      </section>
      <section class="abstract" aria-labelledby="abstract-title">
        <h2 id="abstract-title">Abstract</h2>
        <p>Expressive models. Microsecond planning. <MuMpcLogo /> precompiles learned Koopman dynamics into a compact, action-only optimization problem whose size is independent of the lifted state dimension. Expensive matrix operations move offline; online control uses matrix–vector products and projections, adapting to new goals and constraints without refactorization.</p>
        <p><MuMpcLogo /> reduces planning latency by one to over two orders of magnitude across benchmarks, enabling sub-millisecond visual world model planning, 4096-dimensional quadruped control in under 5 ms, and collision-aware planning for 200 quadrotors at over 30 Hz. The same framework runs onboard a Crazyflie microcontroller, bringing efficient predictive control from embedded robots to high-dimensional learned models.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
        <h2 id="method-title">Method</h2>
        <div class="method-carousel" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Method breakdown" tabindex="0">
          <button class="method-arrow previous" type="button" aria-label="Previous method step" aria-controls="method-slides" disabled>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 6-6 6 6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
          <div id="method-slides">
            {methodSteps.map((step, index) => (
              <figure class="method-card" hidden={index !== 0} role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label={`${index + 1} of ${methodSteps.length}: ${step.title}`}>
                <video muted playsinline preload="auto" aria-label={step.title}>
                  <source src={step.url} type="video/mp4" />
                </video>
                <figcaption class="method-explanation">
                  <h3><span class="method-number">{index + 1} / {methodSteps.length}</span><span>{step.title}</span></h3>
                  <p>{step.explanation.split('μMPC').map((part, partIndex) => <>{partIndex > 0 && <MuMpcLogo />}{part}</>)}</p>
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            ))}
          </div>
          <button class="method-arrow next" type="button" aria-label="Next method step" aria-controls="method-slides">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m10 6 6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
        <h2 id="results-title">Experiments</h2>
        <figure>
          <figcaption><span class="result-number">1 / 5</span><span>Microsecond control.</span></figcaption>
          <img src="/projects/micrompc/assets/results.svg" width="1790" height="713" loading="lazy" alt="Benchmark comparisons of solve times and success rates for quadruped control, linear world models, and 3D quadcopters. μMPC achieves 0.725 ms on bimanual rope planning, 0.427 ms on Reacher, 0.058 ms on CPU quadcopter control, and 32.118 ms for 200 quadcopters." />
        </figure>
        <p class="result-description"><strong>Large models do not have to mean slow control.</strong> Across these benchmarks, <MuMpcLogo /> runs 4096-dimensional quadruped models in milliseconds and 2048-dimensional visual world models in less than one millisecond. For 3D quadcopter control at a 100-step horizon, it reaches 128 μs on CPU: 19× faster than OSQP on the identical condensed QP and over 100× faster than GPU-ADMM SQP on CPU.</p>
        <div class="multi-agent-result">
          <p class="result-summary"><span class="result-number">2 / 5</span><span>Fast, Scalable Multi-Agent Planning</span></p>
          <div class="result-video-pair">
            <figure>
              <video muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="7 physical differential drive robots"><source src={robotariumUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">A.</span> 7 physical differential drive robots</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <video muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="Collision free planning with 150 Quadcopters"><source src={swarmUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">B.</span> Collision free planning with 150 Quadcopters</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p class="result-description"><strong>Four times the agents. Only 2.66× the planning time.</strong> Scaling from 50 to 200 quadrotors raises batched planning latency from 12.1 to 32.1 ms, maintaining over 30 Hz updates and above 98% goal reaching. The 150-agent case shown here takes 23.0 ms. On physical hardware, seven differential-drive robots complete a full five-round update in 18.24 ms on a modest CPU, using just batched NumPy without accelerator libraries such as JAX.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="crazyflie-result">
          <p class="result-summary"><span class="result-number">3 / 5</span><span>Long Horizon (H=75) planning onboard the crazyflie MCU in 24.57 ms</span></p>
          <video muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="Long horizon onboard planning on the Crazyflie microcontroller"><source src={crazyflieUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
          <p class="result-description"><strong>A 75-step lookahead, running on the aircraft’s own microcontroller.</strong> A 128-dimensional learned model plans 1.875 seconds ahead on the Crazyflie’s Cortex–M4F, averaging 24.57 ms per solve during flight with just 8.7 kB of runtime workspace. This onboard deployment solves an unconstrained planning problem; the complete experimental loop runs at about 15 Hz, including communication and state acquisition.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="multi-agent-result">
          <p class="result-summary"><span class="result-number">4 / 5</span><span>Whole-Body Quadruped Planning</span></p>
          <div class="result-video-pair">
            <figure>
              <video class="quadruped-nominal" muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="4096D Koopman planning in 4.47 ms"><source src={quadrupedNomUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">A.</span> 4096D Koopman planning in 4.47 ms</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <video class="quadruped-obstacle" muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="Whole-body obstacle filtering in 28.18 ms"><source src={quadrupedObsUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">B.</span> Whole-body obstacle filtering in 28.18 ms</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p class="result-description"><strong>4096 latent dimensions. Twelve joint torques. Just 4.47 ms.</strong> The model captures the full 61D robot state: base pose and velocity, joint states, foot positions, and ground-reaction forces. Planning directly commands all 12 joint torques; the 25-step timing includes reference generation and state encoding. Extending the horizon to 100 steps takes 13.30 ms. With whole-body obstacle filtering, the 100-step controller still runs in 28.18 ms, avoiding the obstacle crossed by the nominal policy in the evaluated rollouts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="multi-agent-result">
          <p class="result-summary"><span class="result-number">5 / 5</span><span>2048D Linear World Models</span></p>
          <div class="result-video-pair">
            <figure>
              <video class="world-model-video" muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="Hardware cube manipulation"><source src={cubeUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">A.</span> Hardware cube manipulation</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <video class="world-model-video" muted playsinline loop preload="metadata" aria-label="Bimanual rope manipulation in 0.725 ms"><source src={ropeUrl} type="video/mp4" /></video>
              <figcaption><span class="experiment-letter">B.</span> Bimanual rope manipulation in 0.725 ms</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p class="result-description"><strong>A 2048-dimensional world model, planning from pixels in under a millisecond.</strong> Bimanual rope planning takes 0.725 ms with 94% success, versus 559 ms and 46% for Fast-LeWM on the evaluated tasks. Hardware cube manipulation takes 0.483 ms per solve. Differentiable QP supervision recovers the vertical control authority needed to reach the elevated target; prediction-only training falls short. The same visual planning framework also sustains about 30 Hz on Jetson hardware.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="citation" aria-labelledby="citation-title">
        <h2 id="citation-title">Citation</h2>
        <div class="citation-block">
          <pre><code id="citation-text">{`@misc{muMPC_2026,
  title = {μMPC: Safe Nonlinear and World Model Control in Microseconds via Koopman-Linearized Pre-Compilation},
  author = {Nath, Devesh and Chou, Glen},
  note = {Preprint},
  year = {2026}
}`}</code></pre>
          <button class="copy-citation" type="button" aria-label="Copy citation">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      const copyCitation = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy-citation')!;
      copyCitation.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.querySelector('#citation-text')?.textContent ?? '');
          copyCitation.textContent = 'Copied!';
        } catch {
          copyCitation.textContent = 'Unable to copy';
        }
        window.setTimeout(() => { copyCitation.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1500);
      });
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('nav button').forEach((button) => {
        let resetTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;
        button.addEventListener('click', () => {
          clearTimeout(resetTimer);
          button.classList.add('show-soon');
          resetTimer = setTimeout(() => button.classList.remove('show-soon'), 1500);
        });
      });
      const carousel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.method-carousel')!;
      const cards = [...carousel.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.method-card')];
      const previous = carousel.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.previous')!;
      const next = carousel.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.next')!;
      let active = 0;
      let visible = false;
      const finished = new WeakSet<HTMLVideoElement>();
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('#video video, .method-card video').forEach((video) => {
        video.loop = false;
        video.addEventListener('ended', () => {
          finished.add(video);
          video.pause();
        });
      });
      const updatePlayback = () => cards.forEach((card, index) => {
        const video = card.querySelector('video')!;
        if (index === active && visible && !finished.has(video) && !video.ended) video.play().catch(() => {});
        else video.pause();
      });
      const showStep = (index: number) => {
        if (index < 0 || index >= cards.length) return;
        active = index;
        cards.forEach((card, i) => {
          card.hidden = i !== active;
          if (i === active) {
            const video = card.querySelector('video')!;
            finished.delete(video);
            video.currentTime = 0;
          }
        });
        previous.disabled = active === 0;
        next.disabled = active === cards.length - 1;
        updatePlayback();
      };
      previous.addEventListener('click', () => showStep(active - 1));
      next.addEventListener('click', () => showStep(active + 1));
      carousel.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
        if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft' || event.key === 'ArrowRight') {
          event.preventDefault();
          showStep(active + (event.key === 'ArrowLeft' ? -1 : 1));
        }
      });
      new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => {
        visible = entry.isIntersecting;
        updatePlayback();
      }, { threshold: 0.25 }).observe(carousel);
      const resultObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          const video = entry.target as HTMLVideoElement;
          if (entry.isIntersecting) video.play().catch(() => {});
          else video.pause();
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.25 });
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('.results video').forEach((video) => resultObserver.observe(video));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  @font-face { font-family: 'Lato'; src: url('/fonts/Lato-Regular.ttf') format('truetype'); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; }
  @font-face { font-family: 'Lato'; src: url('/fonts/Lato-Bold.ttf') format('truetype'); font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; }
  :global(html) { color-scheme: dark; background: #0a0a0a; min-height: 100%; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; color: #f4f7fb; font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  main { width: min(100% - 64px, 1000px); margin: 0 auto; padding: 80px 0 72px; }
  header { text-align: center; }
  h1 { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 17px; margin: 0 0 34px; font: 700 80px/1 'Lato', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -3px; }
  .subtitle { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.55px; line-height: 1.4; text-wrap: balance; }
  .highlight { color: #50d6ff; }
  .authors { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 15px; margin: 24px 0 0; color: #b7c0c8; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .authors a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .authors a:hover { color: #50d6ff; }
  .authors > span[aria-hidden] { color: #55616c; }
  nav { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 29px 0 48px; }
  nav :is(button, a) { position: relative; isolation: isolate; overflow: hidden; display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 112px; height: 42px; padding: 0; flex: 0 0 112px; border: 1px solid #343c43; border-radius: 24px; background: #1b2025; color: #e5ebef; font: 700 14px/1.4 'Lato', sans-serif; cursor: default; transition: border-color .3s; }
  nav :is(button, a)::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; background: rgb(80 214 255 / 12%); transform: translateY(101%); transition: transform .3s cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1); }
  nav :is(button, a) > span { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; transition: opacity .2s, transform .3s; }
  nav :is(button, a) .resource-label { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 16px 38px; align-content: center; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 8px; line-height: 16px; }
  .resource-label > span { display: block; text-align: left; }
  nav :is(button, a) .soon { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); color: #50d6ff; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .3px; white-space: nowrap; }
  nav :is(button, a):is(:hover, :focus-visible, .show-soon) { border-color: #50d6ff; }
  nav :is(button, a):is(:hover, :focus-visible, .show-soon)::before { transform: translateY(0); }
  nav :is(button, a):is(:hover, :focus-visible, .show-soon) .resource-label { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-8px); }
  nav :is(button, a):is(:hover, :focus-visible, .show-soon) .soon { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  nav a { cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none; }
  nav a:is(:hover, :focus-visible) .resource-label { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  :is(a, button):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #50d6ff; outline-offset: 5px; }
  nav svg { display: block; width: 16px; height: 16px; flex: 0 0 16px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { nav :is(button, a), nav :is(button, a)::before, .resource-label, .soon { transition: none; } }
  #video, .abstract, .method, .results, .citation { position: relative; }
  #video::before, .abstract::before, .method::before, .results::before, .citation::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 1px; background: #50d6ff; }
  #video { scroll-margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 40px; }
  #video h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  video { display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: #000; }
  .abstract { margin: 48px auto 0; padding-top: 40px; }
  .abstract > p { max-width: 760px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .abstract h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 22px; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  .abstract p { text-align: justify; hyphens: auto; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 18px; color: #b7c0c8; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .method { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 40px; }
  .method h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  .method-carousel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px minmax(0, 800px) 44px; gap: 0 24px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  #method-slides { display: contents; }
  .method-card { display: grid; grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 3; grid-template-rows: subgrid; margin: 0; }
  .method-card video { grid-row: 1; }
  .method-arrow { grid-row: 1; align-self: center; }
  .method-arrow.previous { grid-column: 1; }
  .method-arrow.next { grid-column: 3; }
  .method-card[hidden] { display: none; }
  .method-explanation { grid-row: 2; margin: 24px 0 0; }
  .method-explanation p { margin: 0; color: #b7c0c8; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .method-explanation h3 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #f4f7fb; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.4; text-align: center; }
  .method-explanation .method-number { font-weight: 400; white-space: nowrap; }
  .method-number { flex-shrink: 0; color: #50d6ff; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: normal; }
  .method-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 44px; height: 44px; padding: 0; border: 1px solid #343c43; border-radius: 50%; background: #1b2025; color: #e5ebef; cursor: pointer; margin-top: 0; }
  .method-arrow:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #50d6ff; color: #50d6ff; }
  .method-arrow:disabled { opacity: .25; cursor: default; }
  .method-arrow svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .results { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 40px; }
  .results h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  .results figure { margin: 0; }
  .results img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .results figcaption, .result-summary { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; max-width: 860px; margin: 22px auto 0; color: #f4f7fb; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.6; text-align: center; text-wrap: balance; }
  .result-description { max-width: 800px; margin: 24px auto 0; color: #b7c0c8; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .result-description strong { color: #f4f7fb; }
  .result-number { flex-shrink: 0; color: #50d6ff; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: normal; }
  .multi-agent-result, .crazyflie-result { margin-top: 48px; }
  .crazyflie-result video, .quadruped-nominal, .quadruped-obstacle, .world-model-video { background: transparent; }
  .result-video-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; }
  .experiment-letter { color: #50d6ff; margin-right: 6px; }
  .result-video-pair figcaption { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: 16px; }
  .results > figure > figcaption, .result-summary { margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  .citation { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 40px; }
  .citation h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  .citation-block { position: relative; border: 1px solid #2b3035; border-radius: 6px; padding: 20px; }
  .citation pre { width: 100%; min-height: 1.6em; margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; color: #b7c0c8; font: 14px/1.6 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .citation-block .copy-citation { position: absolute; right: 12px; bottom: 12px; }
  .copy-citation { border: 1px solid #343c43; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 12px; background: #1b2025; color: #e5ebef; font: inherit; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; }
  .copy-citation:hover, .copy-citation:focus-visible { border-color: #50d6ff; color: #50d6ff; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    main { width: calc(100% - 36px); padding: 52px 0 36px; }
    h1 { font-size: 64px; gap: 13px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
    .subtitle { font-size: 25px; letter-spacing: -.35px; line-height: 1.4; }
    .authors { margin-top: 23px; font-size: 16px; gap: 12px; }
    nav { gap: 8px; margin: 25px 0 34px; }
    nav :is(button, a) { width: 94px; flex-basis: 94px; }
    #video { padding-top: 28px; }
